Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_dirread.c
Line: 2518
Function: TIFFReadDirEntryLong8ArrayWithLimit
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: Allocates data with size count * 8 without checking for size_t overflow. On 32-bit platforms this multiplication can wrap, leading to an undersized allocation. Subsequent loops write count 64-bit elements into data (e.g., at lines 2533, 2560, 2594, 2609), causing heap buffer overflow. Count is derived from the directory entry and can be attacker-controlled.

Source context:
